<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech fund YSE dives into 1996 loss.</title>
<headline>Czech fund YSE dives into 1996 loss.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech investment fund YSE a.s. posted a loss of 692.7 million crowns after a net profit of 51.2 million in the previous year, according to filings with the Prague Stock Exchange obtained on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Preliminary unaudited results for year ending December 31, 1996: (in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> Net result	     692.696 loss   vs     51.160 profit</p>
<p> Gross result	   692.696 loss   vs     53.389 profit</p>
<p> Opertating result	  n/a	  vs     22.937 loss</p>
<p> Total assets	 3,043.222	  vs  2,794.038</p>
<p> Basic capital	3,452.768	  vs  3,452.768</p>
<p>Note - YSE, originally launched as an investment fund, converted into a holding company last year. Its shares are traded on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange (PSE). The results were calculated according to Czech accounting standards, and were provided by the PSE.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
